note Allen's look: the sky's tables. GENERATED by ~/work/IMacLook/sky/gen_skydata.py from
note native/kernel/ui/sky_data.c (aienux 4b24df65, itself generated by native/kernel/tools/ck_sky_gen.c
note from the Yale Bright Star Catalogue); do not edit the text lines. Decimal numbers, one space between,
note a trailing space. skinit decodes them once into the Sk* pools below; skmake (look-sky.om) calls it.
note Left out on purpose: ck_sky_milkyway, ck_sky_luma, ck_sky_chroma (ck_night_init at 4b24df65 clears the
note sky to black and never calls ck_sky_draw_milkyway: night.c:122-125) and ck_sky_checks (host test only).
note Sdview: ra_mdeg dec_mdeg fov_mdeg roll_mdeg tan_half_q30, then rot_q30 row-major (rows: screen right,
note screen up, the view centre). Sdstars: x y z (Q15, J2000) mag ((V+2)*20) bv (palette index) per star.
note Sdflux: light at the middle of a star of magnitude code m, linear Q16. Sdpal: linear sRGB r g b per
note B-V step, brightest channel 4096. ck_sky_lin / ck_sky_srgb16 (Slin / Ssrgb) are PAINT's: pkinit fills
note them. Sdgal: dir x y z (Q15), a_q16, b_q16, angle
note (turns/65536 from screen right towards down), tint (sRGB packed) per galaxy.
